TD-H3 open firmware
===================

This firmware is MIT (LICENSE), except for the parts below, adapted from Apache-2.0 firmware for
the Quansheng UV-K5 family (the same BK4819 radio chip) and changed for this board and MCU. Those
parts are under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE); each file holding one says so at
its top. Register values found by trying them on the air are facts, used with credit, not code.

What this firmware took, by source
----------------------------------

Dual Tachyon, uv-k5-firmware (https://github.com/DualTachyon/uv-k5-firmware), Copyright 2023
Dual Tachyon:
  - the 55 Hz squelch-tail detector set-up and the REG_02 interrupt acknowledge (fw/bk4819.c).
  - the VOX detector set-up: REG_46, REG_79, REG_7A's low bits, REG_31 bit 2 and its found and lost
    interrupts (fw/bk4819.c, bk_vox_on); the thresholds and the hang are ours.

OneOfEleven, am_fix.c, as carried in https://github.com/armel/uv-k5-firmware-custom,
Copyright 2023 OneOfEleven:
  - the LNA gain steps and five rows of the AM gain table (fw/bk4819.c).

Armel / F4HWN, https://github.com/armel/uv-k5-firmware-custom (register values, fw/bk4819.c,
fw/radio.c):
  - DTMF decode threshold, AM filter width and AGC thresholds, the FM weak-signal filter, mic AGC
    (REG_19), the compander words, the reverse-burst tail (REG_52) and the 6.25 kHz filter.
  - the USB (SSB) receive set-up, from RADIO_SetModulation in radio.c: REG_47 AF type 5, REG_3D
    IF 0 and REG_73 bit 4 (AFC off), changed to our register table code in bk_mode.

muzkr and Armel / F4HWN, the UV-K1 / UV-K5 V3 port,
https://github.com/armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom (register values, fw/bk4819.c):
  - REG_2B's de-emphasis and audio low-pass bits, off in AM.

fagci (https://github.com/fagci), spectrum.c as carried in the UV-K1 / UV-K5 V3 port,
Copyright 2023 fagci:
  - the scope's RSSI read (fw/bk4819.c, bk_dbm_at): wait for the glitch count to settle, then drop
    the first RSSI read, as GetRssi does.

Egzumer (https://github.com/egzumer/uv-k5-firmware-custom): nothing taken; named because the UV-K1
port's NOTICE carries them.

